{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He [Bb]sat by the well in [F]the land of Midian [Bb]
Seven [Eb]daughters came to [Bb]fill the troughs [F]
[Gm]Shepherds drove them a[Eb]way in the heat [Bb]
[Eb]Moses rose up [Bb]to water their flock [F]
[Gm]Reuel asked why [Eb]they returned [Bb]so soon
An [Eb]Egyptian [Bb]had rescued their [F]day
In[Gm]vite him to eat, [Eb]said [Bb]the father
Zip[Eb]porah became his wife that [F]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Blessed be the [F]LORD who rescued [Gm]you
From the [Bb]hand of [F]Pharaoh and E[Eb]gypt
[Gm]Now I know the [F]LORD is grea[Eb]ter
Than all [Cm7]gods who [F]rule the [Bb]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Go in peace, [F]Jethro said to Mo[Bb]ses
Re[Eb]turn to your [Bb]relatives in E[F]gypt
But he [Gm]came back to the [Eb]mountain of [Bb]God
With [Eb]Zipporah and their two [F]sons
[Gm]Gershom, a stranger in [Eb]a foreign [Bb]land
E[Eb]liezer, the [Bb]God of his fa[F]ther
[Gm]Jethro rejoiced [Eb]over the good [Bb]of God
[Eb]He saw the rescue from the Egyp[F]tians
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
