{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]You judge the [Eb]people from morning till [Bb]evening
[Eb]This task is too [Bb]heavy for you a[F]lone
[Gm]Look out for [Eb]capable men [Bb]who fear God
[Eb]Trustworthy men [Bb]who hate a [F]bribe
[Gm]Appoint them over [Eb]thousands and hun[Bb]dreds
[Eb]Fifties and [Bb]tens to judge the peo[F]ple
[Gm]Lighten your load and [Eb]let them car[Bb]ry it
And [Eb]all these people will go home in [F]peace
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Moses listened and [Eb]did everything he [Bb]said
Then [Eb]he sent his fa-ther-in-law home
{end_of_verse}

